ration.ofSeconds(10))\n    .withTimestampAssigner((event, recordTimestamp) -> event.getTimestamp() / 1000);\n    // Note: Flink timestamps are in milliseconds, data timestamps may be in microseconds\n\nDataStream<TaskEvent> withTimestamps = stream.assignTimestampsAndWatermarks(strategy);\n```\n\n### ProcessWindowFunction\nUse `ProcessWindowFunction` for full access to window contents:\n\n```java\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.functions.windowing.ProcessWindowFunction;\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.windowing.windows.TimeWindow;\nimport org.apache.flink.util.Collector;\n\npublic class CountWindowFunction\n    extends ProcessWindowFunction<TaskEvent, Tuple2<Long, Long>, Long, TimeWindow> {\n\n    @Override\n    public void process(Long key, Context context, Iterable<TaskEvent> elements,\n                       Collector<Tuple2<Long, Long>> out) {\n        long count = 0;\n        for (TaskEvent e : elements) {\n            count++;\n        }\n        out.collect(Tuple2.of(key, count));\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Reduce/Aggregate for Finding Max\nAfter windowing, you can use `.reduce()` or `.maxBy()` on a keyed stream to find the session with the most events:\n\n```java\n// After session windowing produces (jobId, count) per session\nsessionCounts\n    .keyBy(t -> t.f0) // key by jobId\n    .reduce((a, b) -> a.f1 > b.f1 ? a : b); // keep the max count\n```\n\n## Tips\n- When reading from a file source, Flink needs watermarks to advance. Use `WatermarkStrategy.forMonotonousTimestamps()` if data is sorted by time, or `forBoundedOutOfOrderness()` otherwise.\n- For finite sources (files), Flink will emit a final watermark of `Long.MAX_VALUE` at end of input, which will close all pending windows.\n- Session windows merge when events arrive within the gap, which can cause window state growth for keys with many sessions.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"06f45dd1-0ba1-4675-b382-4976723fdd38"}
{"parentUuid":"4f27e808-b408-4bb9-b598-cd297f9ed770","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"bd6e6fe0-43d4-4fcd-81ba-1a17927777bb","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"zany-conjuring-pascal","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01Xw7tk5WgLXRf8yAyMzvjf5","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-csv-source-gzip.md"}]},"uuid":"884a748d-3d23-4932-8636-f2186668c6f1","timestamp":"2026-02-07T06:10:56.659Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-csv-source-gzip.md","content":"# Apache Flink - Reading Gzipped CSV Files\n\n## Overview\nReading compressed CSV data as a streaming source in Apache Flink. The data is in gzipped CSV format with no headers.\n\n## Approach: Custom SourceFunction with GZIPInputStream\n\nFor Flink 1.18, a simple approach is to use a custom `SourceFunction` that reads a gzipped CSV file line by line, parses each line, and emits the corresponding POJO/Tuple.\n\n```java\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.functions.source.SourceFunction;\nimport java.io.BufferedReader;\nimport java.io.FileInputStream;\nimport java.io.InputStreamReader;\nimport java.util.zip.GZIPInputStream;\n\npublic class TaskEventSource implements SourceFunction<TaskEvent> {\n    private final String filePath;\n    private volatile boolean isRunning = true;\n\n    public TaskEventSource(String filePath) {\n        this.filePath = filePath;\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public void run(SourceContext<TaskEvent> ctx) throws Exception {\n        try (BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(\n                new InputStreamReader(new GZIPInputStream(new FileInputStream(filePath))))) {\n            String line;\n            while (isRunning && (line = reader.readLine()) != null) {\n                TaskEvent event = TaskEvent.fromCsv(line);\n                if (event != null) {\n                    ctx.collect(event);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public void cancel() {\n        isRunning = false;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## CSV Parsing for Google Cluster Data\n\n### Task Events CSV Format (13 fields)\n```\ntimestamp, missing_info, job_id, task_index, machine_id, event_type, user_name,\nscheduling_class, priority, cpu_request, ram_request, disk_request, different_machine_constraint\n```\n\n### Job Events CSV Format (8 fields)\n```\ntimestamp, missing_info, job_id, event_type, user_name, scheduling_class, job_name, logical_job_name\n```\n\n### Parsing Example\n```java\npublic static TaskEvent fromCsv(String line) {\n    String[] fields = line.split(\",\", -1); // -1 to keep empty trailing fields\n    TaskEvent event = new TaskEvent();\n    event.timestamp = fields[0].isEmpty() ? 0 : Long.parseLong(fields[0]);\n    event.jobId = fields[2].isEmpty() ? 0 : Long.parseLong(fields[2]);\n    event.taskIndex = fields[3].isEmpty() ? 0 : Integer.parseInt(fields[3]);\n    event.eventType = fields[5].isEmpty() ? -1 : Integer.parseInt(fields[5]);\n    return event;\n}\n```\n\n### Important Notes\n- Timestamps are in **microseconds** since 600 seconds before the trace period\n- Fields may be empty (no value), so always check with `isEmpty()` before parsing\n- Event types: SUBMIT(0), SCHEDULE(1), EVICT(2), FAIL(3), FINISH(4), KILL(5), LOST(6), UPDATE_PENDING(7), UPDATE_RUNNING(8)\n- CSV has no header row\n- Use `split(\",\", -1)` to preserve empty trailing fields\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4f27e808-b408-4bb9-b598-cd297f9ed770"}
{"parentUuid":"3f0520f1-476f-4b47-a623-f5028cab4ac3","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"bd6e6fe0-43d4-4fcd-81ba-1a17927777bb","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"zany-conjuring-pascal","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01B8Jp4DWy12iWxHGxzEJHto","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /app/workspace/environment/skills/google-cluster-data-schema.md"}]},"uuid":"dfed7bbb-0fa5-46b0-b941-998eeae13afd","timestamp":"2026-02-07T06:10:56.676Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/app/workspace/environment/skills/google-cluster-data-schema.md","content":"# Google Cluster Data 2011 - Schema Reference\n\n## Overview\nThe Google cluster-usage traces dataset (clusterdata-2011-2) contains 29 days of workload data from a Google compute cell with ~12.5k machines.\n\n## Key Tables for This Task\n\n### Job Events Table\nFields (1-indexed):\n1. **timestamp** (long): microseconds since 600s before trace start\n2. **missing info** (string): why a record was synthesized, empty if original\n3. **job ID** (long): unique job identifier\n4. **event type** (int): event code (see below)\n5. **user name** (string): hashed, opaque\n6. **scheduling class** (int): 0-3, latency sensitivity\n7. **job name** (string): hashed, opaque\n8. **logical job name** (string): hashed, opaque\n\n### Task Events Table\nFields (1-indexed):\n1. **timestamp** (long): microseconds since 600s before trace start\n2. **missing info** (string): empty or code\n3. **job ID** (long): unique job identifier\n4. **task index** (int): 0-based index within job\n5. **machine ID** (long): machine where task was scheduled\n6. **event type** (int): event code (see below)\n7. **user name** (string): hashed\n8. **scheduling class** (int): 0-3\n9. **priority** (int): task priority (0 = lowest)\n10. **CPU request** (float): normalized CPU cores\n11. **RAM request** (float): normalized memory\n12. **disk request** (float): normalized disk space\n13. **different-machine constraint** (boolean as 0/1)\n\n### Event Types\n| Code | Name | Description |\n|------|------|-------------|\n| 0 | SUBMIT | Task/job became eligible for scheduling |\n| 1 | SCHEDULE | Task/job was scheduled on a machine |\n| 2 | EVICT | Descheduled (higher priority, overcommit, etc.) |\n| 3 | FAIL | Descheduled due to failure |\n| 4 | FINISH | Completed normally |\n| 5 | KILL | Cancelled by user/driver/dependency |\n| 6 | LOST | Presumably terminated, record missing |\n| 7 | UPDATE_PENDING | Updated while waiting to be scheduled |\n| 8 | UPDATE_RUNNING | Updated while scheduled |\n\n## Important Notes\n- Timestamps are in **microseconds**\n- Empty fields mean no value is available\n- A job consists of one or more tasks\n- Tasks are identified by (job_id, task_index)\n- If a task fails/is evicted and resubmitted, a new SUBMIT event appears\n- The same task (same job_id + task_index) can be submitted multiple times\n- Flink expects timestamps in milliseconds, so divide by 1000\n\n## Session/Stage Definition (for this task)\n- A \"stage\" = a period of SUBMIT events close together in event time for a given job\n- Stage ends after 10 minutes of inactivity (no SUBMIT events)\n- Count each SUBMIT event separately (resubmissions count as separate events)\n- Find the stage with the highest count of SUBMIT events per job\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3f0520f1-476f-4b47-a623-f5028cab4ac3"}
{"parentUuid":"ebda7e1e-4261-486a-a4f7-2a2d7b09d601","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"bd6e6fe0-43d4-4fcd-81ba-1a17927777bb","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"zany-conjuring-pascal","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01WYbgnBZSxbyUEEFf8xAKzK","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-file-output-sink.md"}]},"uuid":"89a0b2fb-1fe1-4102-9ccd-de234f7d4b62","timestamp":"2026-02-07T06:10:56.698Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-file-output-sink.md","content":"# Apache Flink - Writing Output to Local Files\n\n## Overview\nWriting Flink streaming job results to local files. Multiple approaches depending on Flink version and requirements.\n\n## Approach 1: writeAsText (Simple, Deprecated but Works)\nFor Flink 1.18, the simplest approach for single-file output:\n\n```java\nresult.writeAsText(outputPath, FileSystem.WriteMode.OVERWRITE)\n      .setParallelism(1);  // ensures single output file\n```\n\n**Note:** `writeAsText()` uses `toString()` of each element, so ensure your output type has the correct `toString()` format.\n\n## Approach 2: Using FileSink (Recommended for Production)\n\n```java\nimport org.apache.flink.connector.file.sink.FileSink;\nimport org.apache.flink.api.common.serialization.SimpleStringEncoder;\nimport org.apache.flink.core.fs.Path;\n\nFileSink<String> sink = FileSink\n    .forRowFormat(new Path(outputPath), new SimpleStringEncoder<String>(\"UTF-8\"))\n    .build();\n\nresult.map(t -> t.toString()).sinkTo(sink);\n```\n\n## Approach 3: Custom SinkFunction\n\n```java\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.functions.sink.SinkFunction;\nimport java.io.FileWriter;\nimport java.io.PrintWriter;\n\npublic class FileSinkFunction implements SinkFunction<String> {\n    private final String path;\n    private transient PrintWriter writer;\n\n    public FileSinkFunction(String path) {\n        this.path = path;\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public void invoke(String value, Context context) throws Exception {\n        if (writer == null) {\n            writer = new PrintWriter(new FileWriter(path, true));\n        }\n        writer.println(value);\n        writer.flush();\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format for This Task\nOutput should be `(jobId,count)` format, one per line. Using `Tuple2<Long, Long>`:\n\n```java\n// Tuple2.toString() produces \"(value1,value2)\" which matches the required format\nDataStream<Tuple2<Long, Long>> result = ...;\nresult.writeAsText(outputPath, FileSystem.WriteMode.OVERWRITE).setParallelism(1);\n```\n\n## Important Notes\n- Set parallelism to 1 for single output file\n- `Tuple2.toString()` produces format `(f0,f1)` which matches `(first_int,second_int)`\n- Use `FileSystem.WriteMode.OVERWRITE` to handle re-runs\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ebda7e1e-4261-486a-a4f7-2a2d7b09d601"}
{"parentUuid":"752d6fe3-6896-4879-bcb4-9d9b5d1ff2ce","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"bd6e6fe0-43d4-4fcd-81ba-1a17927777bb","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"zany-conjuring-pascal","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01PJynUt4oXp2UtnYj6Feut2","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-keyed-stream-aggregation.md"}]},"uuid":"4f312811-e784-4cdd-928b-3fd232600f28","timestamp":"2026-02-07T06:10:56.716Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/app/workspace/environment/skills/flink-keyed-stream-aggregation.md","content":"# Apache Flink - Keyed Stream Aggregation Patterns\n\n## Overview\nPatterns for aggregating data over keyed streams in Flink, including finding max values per key across multiple windows.\n\n## Pattern: Session Window + Max Aggregation\n\n### Step 1: Filter and Key\n```java\nDataStream<TaskEvent> submits = taskEvents\n    .filter(e -> e.eventType == 0)  // SUBMIT events only\n    .keyBy(e -> e.jobId);\n```\n\n### Step 2: Session Window to Count Events per Session\n```java\nDataStream<Tuple2<Long, Long>> sessionCounts = submits\n    .keyBy(e -> e.jobId)\n    .window(EventTimeSessionWindows.withGap(Time.minutes(10)))\n    .process(new ProcessWindowFunction<TaskEvent, Tuple2<Long, Long>, Long, TimeWindow>() {\n        @Override\n        public void process(Long jobId, Context ctx, Iterable<TaskEvent> elements,\n                           Collector<Tuple2<Long, Long>> out) {\n            long count = 0;\n            for (TaskEvent e : elements) {\n                count++;\n            }\n            out.collect(Tuple2.of(jobId, count));\n        }\n    });\n```\n\n### Step 3: Find Max Count per Job\n```java\nDataStream<Tuple2<Long, Long>> maxPerJob = sessionCounts\n    .keyBy(t -> t.f0)\n    .reduce((a, b) -> a.f1 > b.f1 ? a : b);\n```\n\n## Alternative: Using ReduceFunction with ProcessWindowFunction\n```java\n// More efficient: incrementally reduce within the window\n.window(EventTimeSessionWindows.withGap(Time.minutes(10)))\n.reduce(\n    (a, b) -> { a.count++; return a; },  // incremental reduce\n    new ProcessWindowFunction<>() { ... }  // finalize\n);\n```\n\n## KeyBy with Tuple2\nWhen working with `Tuple2`, use field position or lambda:\n```java\n// By field position\nstream.keyBy(0);  // deprecated in newer Flink\n\n// By lambda (preferred)\nstream.keyBy(t -> t.f0);\n\n// By KeySelector\nstream.keyBy(new KeySelector<Tuple2<Long, Long>, Long>() {\n    @Override\n    public Long getKey(Tuple2<Long, Long> value) {\n        return value.f0;\n    }\n});\n```\n\n## Important: Type Information\nFlink needs type information for serialization. When using lambdas with generic types, you may need `.returns()`:\n```java\nstream.keyBy(e -> e.jobId)\n    .window(...)\n    .process(...)\n    .returns(TypeInformation.of(new TypeHint<Tuple2<Long, Long>>() {}));\n```\n\n## Parallelism Considerations\n- The final `reduce` operates on a keyed stream, so output may have multiple partitions\n- Set `.setParallelism(1)` on the sink to get a single output file\n- Reduce on a keyed stream produces one output per key when the stream finishes (for bounded sources)\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"752d6fe3-6896-4879-bcb4-9d9b5d1ff2ce"}
