ent> elements,\n                                        Collector<Tuple2<Long, Long>> out) {\n                        long count = 0;\n                        for (TaskEvent e : elements) {\n                            count++;\n                        }\n                        out.collect(Tuple2.of(jobId, count));\n                    }\n                });\n\n        // Find the max session count per job using a KeyedProcessFunction.\n        // Track max in state and emit only once at end of stream via an event-time\n        // timer set to Long.MAX_VALUE - 1, which fires when the final watermark arrives.\n        DataStream<Tuple2<Long, Long>> maxPerJob = sessionCounts\n                .keyBy(t -> t.f0)\n                .process(new KeyedProcessFunction<Long, Tuple2<Long, Long>, Tuple2<Long, Long>>() {\n                    private transient ValueState<Long> maxCount;\n                    private transient ValueState<Boolean> timerRegistered;\n\n                    @Override\n                    public void open(Configuration parameters) {\n                        maxCount = getRuntimeContext().getState(\n                                new ValueStateDescriptor<>(\"maxCount\", Types.LONG));\n                        timerRegistered = getRuntimeContext().getState(\n                                new ValueStateDescriptor<>(\"timerRegistered\", Types.BOOLEAN));\n                    }\n\n                    @Override\n                    public void processElement(Tuple2<Long, Long> value, Context ctx,\n                                               Collector<Tuple2<Long, Long>> out) throws Exception {\n                        Long current = maxCount.value();\n                        if (current == null || value.f1 > current) {\n                            maxCount.update(value.f1);\n                        }\n                        // Register a timer at max watermark to emit final result\n                        if (timerRegistered.value() == null) {\n           